    "bic_delta": -18759.24,
    "bic_note": "AIC and BIC both improved substantially (lower is better): AIC delta = -24754, BIC delta = -18759. This reflects the large improvement in training log-likelihood from 628 interaction terms. However, AIC/BIC are not reliable for rank-deficient models — they assume the model is well-identified, which is violated here. The training improvement captured by AIC/BIC is real but corresponds to overfitting, not genuine signal extraction.",
    "interpretation": "Catastrophic test performance (R² = -42.16, RMSE = 14.52 vs additive RMSE = 1.09). Train R² improved by +0.0487 while test R² collapsed. Cause: rank-deficient model with 628 interaction terms memorizes training patterns; many product × vendor and product × state interactions are specific to training data. AIC/BIC show improvement but are not valid for rank-deficient fits."
  },
  "part_f_recommendation": {
    "decision": "KEEP_ADDITIVE_BASELINE",
    "justification": "OLS_INTERACTION_FULL achieves delta test R² = -42.9162 vs OLS_ADDITIVE_FINAL (0.7552 → -42.1610). Out-of-sample performance collapses: the model fails catastrophically on held-out data due to a rank-deficient fit (R warning: 'prediction from rank-deficient fit; doubtful cases'). AIC and BIC both improved numerically (AIC delta = -24754, BIC delta = -18759) but are not reliable for a rank-deficient model — the training log-likelihood improvement reflects overfitting of 628 interaction terms, not generalizable signal. Complexity expanded from 48 to 676 estimated coefficients with 82 aliased. Recommend retaining OLS_ADDITIVE_FINAL as the OLS specification. Note: log_prev_wp:PROD_ABBR interactions show strong signal in isolation (|t| > 40 for GARAGE, WORKCOMP) and may merit a targeted future test."
  }
